    "The races of CustomRaces.Races can be created and played. Needs a restart.\n    Off: none of them; their characters play their base race until they are on again.\nDefault:     1 - Enabled\n    0 - Disabled": "",
    "The races that are playable, by their key (the English name without spaces), separated by\n    spaces, for example \"Goblin Worgen Vrykul\". Each needs its options below.\n    None is chosen by default: each realm picks its own.\nDefault:     \"\"": "",
    "Race numbers above 31 (up to 63), for more than the 31 races the game client knows. Needs the\n    64-race patch of the game client (dinput8.dll next to Ascension.exe; CoA Custom ships one) in the\n    game of every player, and the core change of this module. AFK Realm puts the DLL of\n    CustomRaces.MoreRacesFile next to the game while this is on (Modules > Game client > Install) and\n    into the ZIP for the other players. A race above 32 has no bit of its own in race masks: it does\n    what its base race may do (quests, items, skills).\nDefault:     0 - Off\n    1 - On": "",
    "The 64-race patch (dinput8.dll) to put next to the game. AFK Realm keeps it in the race\n    folder (_Client\\dinput8.dll) when it makes race packs from CoA Custom.\nDefault:     \"\"": "",
    "The files of CoA Custom that belong next to Ascension.exe: its folder files\\client_root\n    (Ascension-b.exe, EsteriaAppearance.dll with its .bin files, cursors). AFK Realm copies all\n    of them next to the game when it installs the client patch (Modules > Game client > Install)\n    and takes them away again when this is emptied; a file of the same name that was there\n    before is kept as <name>.afk-backup. They do not go into the ZIP for the other players,\n    who have the client of CoA Custom themselves. Not read by the server.\nDefault:     \"\"": ""
  }
}
